				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "30a9a178-6a4f-4fd6-999c-9adecf7cbc44")
	)
	(text "Suitable MOSFETs for H-bridge:\n\nC3288282-MCAC95N06Y\nC7220836-BSC010N04LS6ATMA1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.3 133.35 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "394635ba-61b0-4435-9e43-66f2d241d35c")
	)
	(text "Suggested steps in testing:\n1. Characterize the baseline (as-populated pure PI) first: step response settling time, overshoot, steady-state accuracy, and current noise floor, \n   across a couple of coils spanning your inductance range if available.\n2. Add R3 only, re-measure the same metrics, specifically checking windup recovery behavior.\n3. Remove R3, add Rd+C5 only, re-measure, specifically checking settling speed/overshoot vs. noise floor.\n4. Only combine both if a specific problem observed in step 1 motivates it - don't stack tuning options speculatively.\nGeneral sizing guidelines are included below"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9e3413ac-c3f0-41b7-8702-5c7e7514f1ec")
	)
	(text "Compensation Network:\n~2ms response time\n\nR3 helps resolve windup problem (visible overshoot/ringing after intentionally forcing the loop into current limit and releasing it)\nTradeoff: costs steady state precision\nSizing: 10M~1M (Higher value -> slower windup recovery but minimal steady state error)\n\nC5 and R23 helps resolve ringing/overshoot due to insufficient phase margin\nTradeoff: noise performance drops\nC5 Sizing: ~150nF\nR23 Sizing: 470~560"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 68.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a65a4abc-7b21-402a-966d-8cd6df54b216")
	)
	(text "Resistors pads: 0603 package\nCapcitor pads: 0805 package"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.7 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f4b44352-27d1-42e2-838d-1cb67a91b98c")
	)
